## Overview

Implement runtime behavior for broadcast and role channels in MessageRouter, plus priority-based wake/interrupt decisions.

## Design: Gastown Three-Tier Subscription Model

### Tier 1: Automatic Role-Based Subscriptions

Agents auto-subscribe to their role channel at spawn time:
```typescript
// At agent spawn, auto-subscribe to @{role} channel
if (agent.role) {
  messageRouter.subscribe(agent.id, { type: 'role', role: agent.role });
}
```

### Tier 2: Explicit Topic Subscriptions

Agents explicitly subscribe/unsubscribe:
```typescript
// Agent calls subscribe for topics they care about
messageRouter.subscribe(agentId, { type: 'topic', topic: 'alerts' });
messageRouter.unsubscribe(agentId, { type: 'topic', topic: 'alerts' });
```

### Tier 3: Blanket Broadcast with Scope Filtering

Broadcast to all with optional scope:
```typescript
messageRouter.send({
  to: { type: 'broadcast', scope: 'workers' }, // or 'all', 'coordinators', 'monitors'
  content: 'System maintenance in 5 minutes',
});
```

